cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below and cite the references it builds on."
type: software
title: "OIT on the Compatibility renderer: CPU models and comparison harnesses (entities-godot, dev/oit-compat)"
authors:
  - name: "weftspun"
    alias: "fire"
    website: "https://github.com/fire"
  - family-names: "Lee"
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    alias: "fire"
    website: "https://github.com/fire"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  CPU models and harnesses for fragment-only order-independent transparency on
  Godot's Compatibility (GLES3 / WebGL2) renderer: the froxel design of the
  RenderingDevice renderers without compute shaders, storage buffers or atomics
  (a packed four-slices-a-texel scan, the engine's auto-range and depth intervals),
  compared against depth-peeled sorting and weighted blended OIT on an exact
  back-to-front composite. The GL passes themselves are not written yet.
references:
  - type: software
    title: "VRChat Gaussian Splatting"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Moroz"
        given-names: "Mykhailo"
    url: "https://github.com/MichaelMoroz/VRChatGaussianSplatting"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/MichaelMoroz/VRChatGaussianSplatting"
    commit: "b9e3db370ce017460eeb96e70ddc6a7c3eeb48c1"
    date-released: "2026-08-31"
    license: MIT
    notes: >-
      Read for its technique, not copied: a radix sort and prefix sums built
      from mipmaps with only ordinary rasterization (RadixSort/RadixSort.shader,
      RadixSort/Utils.cginc), the same limits as a WebGL2 fragment pipeline.
      No code from it is in this repository.
  - type: software
    title: "CompactSparseTextureDemo"
    authors:
      - name: "d4rkc0d3r"
    url: "https://github.com/d4rkc0d3r/CompactSparseTextureDemo"
    license: MIT
    notes: "The mipmap prefix-sum trick that the Gaussian splatting radix sort credits."
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "Adaptive Volumetric Boundary Order-Independent Transparency"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Drobot"
        given-names: "Michał"
    conference:
      name: "SIGGRAPH 2025, Advances in Real-Time Rendering in Games"
    url: "https://advances.realtimerendering.com/s2025/content/AVBOIT_SIG2025_MDROBOT-final.pdf"
    year: 2025
  - type: software
    title: "entities-godot"
